    <statement><p>Consider the following functions <m>f: \lbrace 1,2,3,4,5\rbrace \to \lbrace 1,2,3\rbrace</m>.  For each, determine whether it is (only) injective, (only) surjective, bijective, or neither injective nor surjective.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>f = \begin{pmatrix}1 \amp  2 \amp  3 \amp  4 \amp  5 \\ 2 \amp  2 \amp  3 \amp  3 \amp  2\end{pmatrix}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f = \begin{pmatrix}1 \amp  2 \amp  3 \amp  4 \amp  5 \\ 2 \amp  1 \amp  2 \amp  1 \amp  2\end{pmatrix}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f(x) = \begin{cases} 4-x \amp  \text{ if } x \le 3 \\ x-3 \amp  \text{ if } x &gt; 3 \end{cases}</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
